I wanted to report a small bug when using the function `chat_structured` function in combination with `type_from_schema` with a deeply nested JSON schema. This is related to issue #529.

It seems that there is an openAI schema limitation that does not allow for object nesting deeper than 5 levels. If you use more levels than that, you get an error like this:
```
ℹ : Invalid schema for response_format 'structured_data': 6 levels of nesting exceeds limit of 5.
```
However, what I found is that the current implementation of the `chat_structured` function contains the following lines:

```
needs_wrapper <- S7_inherits(private$provider, ProviderOpenAI)
type <- wrap_type_if_needed(type, needs_wrapper)
```
The result is that the passed schema is wrapped one more time as an object. This results in one more additional nesting level, that should not be there.

I confirmed that if I manually set  `needs_wrapper <- FALSE`, then the `structured_chat` call works fine.


Here is a reprex that you can use as a test for this behavior.

```
chat <- chat_openai(model = "o3",  system_prompt = "You are a baker")

recipe <- "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C)."

result <- chat$chat_structured(recipe,
                               type = ellmer::type_from_schema('{
  "title": "Cookie Schema",
  "description": "Test",
  "type": "object",
  "required":["recipes"],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties":{
    "recipes": {
      "type": "array",
      "description": "List of detailed information on each of recipes",
      "items":{
        "type": "object",
        "description": "Detailed information about a specific recipe.",
        "required": [ "equipment"],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "equipment": {
            "type": "array",
            "description": "Detailed list of all equipment required.",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "details": {
                  "type":"object",
                  "description": "Specifications and operating conditions.",
                  "required": ["specification"],
                  "additionalProperties": false,
                  "properties": {
                    "specification": {
                      "type": "object",
                      "description": "Equipment specifications like temperature range",
                      "required": ["temperature"],
                      "additionalProperties": false,
                      "properties": {
                        "temperature": {"type": "string", "description": "e.g., 100F, 500F"}
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              },
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "required": ["details"]
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
'))
```

This is the expected result for the example above. I see this when setting the `needs_wrapper <- FALSE` inside the `chat_structured` function.

```
$recipes
$recipes[[1]]
$recipes[[1]]$equipment
$recipes[[1]]$equipment[[1]]
$recipes[[1]]$equipment[[1]]$details
$recipes[[1]]$equipment[[1]]$details$specification
$recipes[[1]]$equipment[[1]]$details$specification$temperature
