I am building a demo shiny app using a google vertex ai oauth integration in Connect and found that when using `ellmer::chat_google_vertex` inside of a `shiny::moduleServer`, the function fails to detect that it's running within a Posit Connect environment, causing authentication to fail.

I *think*  that the issue occurs because `shiny::moduleServer` creates a namespace-scoped session object that is isolated from the parent application's session.  When `ellmer::chat_google_vertex` internally calls `default_google_credentials()` which in turn calls `has_connect_viewer_token()`, it isn't operating within the parent session and thus returns FALSE.

### Code

When deployed to Connect, the following app crashes with the error log: `No Google credentials are available.`

```R
library(shiny)
library(ellmer)
library(bslib)
library(connectcreds)

app_ui <- function(id) {
  bslib::page_sidebar(
    sidebar = shinychat::chat_ui("chat", height = "300px")
  )
}

chat_server <- function(id) {

  shiny::moduleServer(
    id,
    function(input, output, session) {

      current_chat <- 
        ellmer::chat_google_vertex(
          location = "us-central1",
          project_id = "xxxxxx",
          model = "gemini-2.5-flash"
        )

      shiny::observeEvent(input$chat_user_input, {

        stream <- current_chat$stream_async(input$chat_user_input)
        shinychat::chat_append("chat", stream)

        }
      )

      list(chat = current_chat)

    }
  )

}

ui <- shiny::fluidPage(
  app_ui("test")
)

server <- function(input, output, session) {
  chat_server("test")
}

shiny::shinyApp(ui, server)

```

